# File Size Limits

Apply these limits to files the agent creates or edits. Existing over-limit files are not retroactively split unless they are touched.

| File type | Limit | Required response when exceeded |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Python (`*.py`) | 300 lines | Split into focused modules under an appropriate package, with a thin orchestrator if needed. |
| Markdown (`*.md`) | 500 lines | Split into a folder with `00_index.md` plus one file per major section. |

## Markdown Exemption

Files under `report/output/**` are exempt from the 500-line Markdown limit because they are report deliverables, assembled chapters, writing controls, or export artifacts.

## Enforcement

- Before finishing, count lines on every touched Python or Markdown file.
- If a touched file is over its limit, split it in the same change.
- If splitting is genuinely inappropriate, call out the reason explicitly in the final response or commit message.
